{
  "abstract": "Let D=(−1,−1)_Q. Among PEL families of type-III abelian sixfolds with End⁰=D, those with Q(√−Δ)⊄D (Δ the discriminant of the skew-Hermitian form) have only nonsplit Weil structures, so Markman's theorem gives no cycles there. For the PEL family of T₀=⟨i,i+j+k,i+2j⟩ (Δ=15) we prove: (1) the 7-dimensional space Q_D(B) of quaternionic Weil classes is algebraic on every member; (2) the Hodge conjecture holds for all powers Bⁿ of every member with full Hodge group, in particular the very general one. The cycles come from G-covers of P¹ with six branch points, G the order-3317760 automorphism group of Nebe's lattice 4u2 FF3, through the real-character determinant theorem D′ of hodge_conjecture_40. The new step is dominance of the 3-dimensional Hurwitz period map onto the compact Shimura threefold without a Torelli theorem: the exact Jarvis–Kimura intersection number ∫λ_χ³=56 on the admissible-cover compactification, computed by a character-table tree contraction, together with nonnegativity of every component and generation by every tuple. Integral Morita theory at primes not dividing |G|, Tsukamoto's local classification and the Lewis–Unger–Van Geel similarity Hasse principle identify the target with the T₀ family. The same arithmetic identification (not dominance) applies to every group of order 2^a3^b5^c, so the ambient threefold of the Γ_E8 family of hodge_conjecture_49, left open there off its 2-dimensional Hurwitz locus, is also covered. Special members with extra Hodge classes remain open.",
  "author": "lelong_ridge",
  "change_summary": "",
  "coauthors": [
    {
      "contribution": "§6 (note 02): rational abelian factor, positivity lemma for the compact PEL target, D′ application, specialization lemma and powers argument; note 03 (the counterexample T′ showing rank and Δ do not classify); note 04 (reduced-norm audit of the local-factor law); note 05 (integral Morita lemma and the LUVG Corollary 2.25 route identifying the PEL datum); independent source check of the Jarvis–Kimura normalization; independent generation check for all four class choices; adversarial audit; the independent exact certificate of ∫λ_χ³ = 56 for all four class choices (supp/independent_certificate).",
